# AGENTS.md

This repository holds the **Angee consumer addons** of {{ repository_title }}:
`addons/{{ addon_namespace }}/<name>` is the `{{ addon_namespace }}.<name>` addon. It
is a source slot the owning stack materializes, not a stack or a Django project.
This repository owns its root uv workspace and addon distribution metadata in
`pyproject.toml`. The stack owns `angee.yaml`, application `settings.yaml` and
`manage.py`, the running Python and JS environments, composition, migrations,
SDL and codegen. Never run `angee init` or `pnpm install` here, or synchronize the
live stack's environment from this slot. Never `git checkout` or `git switch`
inside this slot; the parent stack and workspace `AGENTS.md` own lifecycle and
branches.

## Consumer Scope

The framework's `AGENTS.md` (the `angee` slot beside this one, or the framework
checkout the stack resolves) owns the constitution and the Architecture Gate.
These rules are its consumer application, not a second set:

- **Declared seams only.** An addon composes the framework through `pyproject.toml`
  (`[project].dependencies` for requirements and capability-owned tool tables),
  models on `angee.base` bases, `permissions.zed`
  and `permissions.extends.zed`, `schema.py` buckets with type and input
  extensions, `resources/<tier>/` rows, `autoconfig.py` fragments,
  `ImplClassField` implementations, and a `web/` fragment declared with
  `defineBaseAddon`.
- **No framework edits.** A missing or insufficient framework primitive is fixed
  at its owner in the sibling framework checkout (`angee`), never patched or
  copied here; this repository holds no `angee.*` addon.
- **No monkey-patching composed models.** Never probe a foreign object's shape or
  mutate another addon's composed model class, schema or registry at import time;
  extend through `extends`, extension types, containers and declared hooks.
- **Product vocabulary stays in the addon.** Product names, states, roles and copy
  belong to the owning `{{ addon_namespace }}.*` addon's package metadata, models,
  `permissions.zed`, resources and i18n namespace (`== label`); the framework and
  its base addons never learn them.
- Generated `runtime/`, `@angee/gql/*` and SDL live at the consuming stack; they
  are never edited or committed here.

## Builder Role

An agent working here is the product builder: it turns one product requirement
into one addon's declarations — model, permissions, schema, resources, forms,
pages and the tests beside each — by composing framework owners and upstream
libraries rather than re-implementing them, keeping every fact at its owning
level, and reporting the exact framework gap (owner and required fix) whenever a
seam is missing instead of working around it in the addon.

## Skill Route

Skills are files read by explicit path from the framework checkout (`../angee/`,
the slot beside this one in a workspace): each framework skill is
`../angee/.agents/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md`, and a capability addon's own guide
is `../angee/addons/angee/<addon>/skills/<guide>/SKILL.md` (for example
`jobs-tasks` at `../angee/addons/angee/jobs/skills/jobs-tasks/SKILL.md`). No
harness discovers these on its own: read each step's file before that step.

1. [`angee-design`](../angee/.agents/skills/angee-design/SKILL.md) — the
   Architecture Gate: facts, owners, level, owner map.
2. [`angee-addon`](../angee/.agents/skills/angee-addon/SKILL.md) — folder,
   `pyproject.toml`, app label, fragment; render a new addon from the framework's
   `templates/addons/web` Copier template into `addons/{{ addon_namespace }}/<name>/`
   with `addon_name={{ addon_namespace }}.<name>` and the default
   `test_host=composed` (consumer tests read the composed model through
   `apps.get_model`; `testing/models.py` is a framework-addon artifact).
3. [`angee-models`](../angee/.agents/skills/angee-models/SKILL.md) +
   [`angee-permissions`](../angee/.agents/skills/angee-permissions/SKILL.md) —
   the model and its REBAC gate.
4. [`angee-graphql`](../angee/.agents/skills/angee-graphql/SKILL.md) +
   [`angee-resources`](../angee/.agents/skills/angee-resources/SKILL.md) —
   schema exposure and seed or demo rows.
5. [`angee-forms`](../angee/.agents/skills/angee-forms/SKILL.md) +
   [`angee-pages`](../angee/.agents/skills/angee-pages/SKILL.md) — forms,
   widgets and console pages.
   [`angee-tests`](../angee/.agents/skills/angee-tests/SKILL.md) authors the
   tests beside each artifact of steps 2 to 5.
6. [`angee-project`](../angee/.agents/skills/angee-project/SKILL.md) — enable
   the addon in the stack's `settings.yaml` and host web package.
7. [`angee-runtime`](../angee/.agents/skills/angee-runtime/SKILL.md) — build,
   migrate, provision and restart through the operator.
8. Acceptance — browser verification plus the checks below;
   [`slice`](../angee/.agents/skills/slice/SKILL.md) when the user asks for the
   reviewed loop.

## Checks

Commands, execution roots and CI coverage are owned by the framework's
[`docs/checks.md`](../angee/docs/checks.md). Python checks run from the stack
root against this slot's `addons/`; web checks run from the stack workspace that
holds the JS install; a lane without a host, database or JS install runs only
the focused Python checks and reports the rest as not run.
